{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q015_artifact_tag_not_homology\",\"answer\":\"d1a14h2 is the synthetic eight-residue N-terminal tag of PDB 1a14 chain H, separated from the biological d1a14h1 segment (H:9-111; b.1.1.1). SCOPe 2.08 assigns d1a14h2 to class l, Artifacts; fold l.1, Tags; superfamily l.1.1, Tags; family l.1.1.1, Tags; protein “N-terminal Tags”; species “Synthetic.” Similarity confined to this tag is therefore evidence only of reused construct engineering, not evolutionary homology between the associated proteins. It must not support function transfer, biological-domain/fold assignment, template selection, clustering, or representative selection; those conclusions require evidence from the non-tag protein region, with the tag masked or excluded.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"/api/v1/releases\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08\",\"/api/v1/\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/d1a14h2\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/343393\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/311501\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310894\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310359\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310358\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310357\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310682\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310607\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310573\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/310555\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1a14\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1a14/domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1a14/chains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2\"]}]}"}}
